{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>to increase for you its yield.</b> This commandment that you keep — it will be to increase for you its yield, for in its reward I bless you with the fruits of the planting. Rabbi Akiva would say: the Torah spoke against the evil inclination — lest a person say, 'Four years I have toiled in it for nothing!' Therefore it says, 'to increase for you its yield' (Sifra)." "<b>I am YHWH.</b> I am YHWH, who promises this and is trustworthy to fulfill His promise."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:07:12.284568531Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}